never take it. This specifies a finite fallback where the original
supplier left post-noncanonical behavior unspecified.

The common return appends the actual current frame to completed-frames
by AppendItem, updates its descriptor-backed bank, performs the specified
outcome publication/acknowledgement, and restores Ready by a CTL. New
service handlers use no further IN. The source path's original output is
acknowledged before this return; a service outcome uses Definition 13.4.
The next frame is not admitted during either path. There is no optional
idle or return scheduling choice to be inferred later from the clock.

